PDP-8a Programmer's Panel
<UL>
<LI><b>8235.sch</b> is a schematic for an approximation of the function of
the unobtainium 8235 chip.</LI>
<LI><b>8235sub.sch</b> is a schematic for an approximation of the function of
the unobtainium 8235 chip.</LI>
<LI><b>8235sub1.sch</b> is a schematic for an approximation of the function of
the unobtainium 8235 chip.</LI>
<LI><b>8235sub2.sch</b> is a schematic for an approximation of the function of
the unobtainium 8235 chip.</LI>
<LI><b>programmerconsole.sch</b> is a schematic (before board layout) of 
an early draft of board1.</LI>
<LI><b>programmerconsolebrd2.sch</b> is a schematic (before board layout) of
an early draft of board1.</LI>
<LI><b>try1</b> is an early draft (05/26/2005) of board1 (the front-side
board).</LI>
<LI><b>try2</b> is an early draft (05/27/2005) of board2 (the back-side
board).</LI>
<LI><b>cut</b> is the stuff cut from board 1 and pasted to start board2, to
ensure size and alignment match up.
<LI><b>oboard2</b> is a checkpoint of an old version (06/02/2005) of
board2.</LI>
<LI><b>Progpanl.fpd</b> is a Front Panel Express drawing of the Programmer's
Panel artwork.</LI>
<LI><b>nosilkboth.brd</b> is both boards panelized, which is how the prototypes
were ordered.  This version has not had the silkscreen scripts run.</LI>
<LI><b>both.brd</b> is both boards panelized, which is how the prototypes
were ordered.  This version has had the silkscreen scripts run.</LI>
<LI><b>board1-0</b> is a snapshot of revision 0 of board1.</LI>
<LI><b>board2-0</b> is a snapshot of revision 0 of board2.</LI>
<LI><b>board1corrected</b> is board1 with the corrections to make DEC's
schematics work.</LI>
<LI><b>board2corrected</b> is board2 with the corrections to make DEC's
schematics work. (Has a consistency problem.)</LI>
<LI><b>board2eco</b> is board2 with the ECO's applied to make it work.
(Has a consistency problem which highlights the ECOs.)</LI>
<LI><b>board1</b> is the latest drawing of board 1 (front) of the 8/A front
panel replacement.</LI>
<LI><b>board2</b> is the latest drawing of board 2 (back) of the 8/A front
panel replacement.</LI>
